<p>The patch track grades against maintainer reference behavior. These case=
 studies show source-level agent patches stripped out of their larger gener=
ated workspaces.</p>
<ul>
<li><code>oss-fuzz:435781342</code> (<code>libxml2</code>) contrasts sympto=
m-level namespace handling patches in <code>SAX2.c</code> with GPT-5.5=E2=
=80=99s passing <code>parserInternals.c</code> lifecycle fix.</li>
<li><code>oss-fuzz:416295951</code> (<code>opensc</code>) shows DeepSeek, G=
rok 4.3, and GPT-5.5 passing with compact <code>card-oberthur.c</code> resp=
onse-buffer patches, alongside the maintainer=E2=80=99s broader <code>card-=
nqApplet.c</code> and <code>iso7816.c</code> fix.</li>
<li><strong>Takeaway:</strong> local patches can pass when they block the c=
rash path, but the reference patch often shows the broader invariant mainta=
iners chose to encode.</li>
</ul>
