<h2 id=3D"provider-side-refusals">Provider-side refusals</h2>
<p>Some providers may refuse vulnerability-style prompts even in authorized=
 benchmark sandboxes. We count these as measurable failures.</p>
<p>Exact refusal/filter counts from the published-run evidence in this prev=
iew:</p>
<ul>
<li>Claude Fable 5: PoC <strong>60/60 all-chain refusals</strong>; Patch <s=
trong>N/A</strong> (no Patch run in this preview).</li>
<li><a href=3D"https://www.vals.ai/models/anthropic_claude-opus-5" class=3D=
"model-highlight">Claude Opus 5</a>: PoC <strong>1/60 successful fallback r=
esponse</strong> after a primary refusal and <strong>59/60 all-chain refusa=
ls</strong>; Patch <strong>0/61</strong>. The successful-fallback task late=
r errored, so all 60 PoC tasks score <strong>0.00%</strong>.</li>
<li><a href=3D"https://www.vals.ai/models/anthropic_claude-opus-4-7" class=
=3D"model-highlight">Claude Opus 4.7</a>: PoC <strong>34 refusal-like task =
errors</strong> (<strong>35 total task errors</strong>); Patch <strong>0 re=
fusal-like task errors</strong>.</li>
<li><a href=3D"https://www.vals.ai/models/anthropic_claude-opus-4-8" class=
=3D"model-highlight">Claude Opus 4.8</a>: PoC <strong>30 refusal-like task =
errors</strong> (<strong>34 total task errors</strong>); Patch <strong>0 re=
fusal-like task errors</strong>.</li>
<li><a href=3D"https://www.vals.ai/models/alibaba_qwen3.7-plus" class=3D"mo=
del-highlight">Qwen 3.7 Plus</a>: PoC <strong>59 <code>data_inspection_fail=
ed</code> task errors</strong> (<strong>60/60 failed</strong>); Patch <stro=
ng>5 <code>data_inspection_failed</code> task errors</strong> (<strong>7 to=
tal task errors</strong>).</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<p>NOTE: We benchmark models on 60 tasks that were harvested after CyberGym=
=E2=80=99s original task window. We plan to
add more tasks to further capture models=E2=80=99 capabilities here. As we =
add more tasks, we may also add a new track and/or
make updates to the evaluation mechanism.</p>
